# prompt: Pins LF line endings so contributions are stored byte for byte (founder: "init git in this folder so we start saving"). Revision 2 stops treating binary files as text: "* text eol=lf" converted line endings inside a PNG and corrupted it. Revision 3 stores exported evidence byte for byte, so its recorded hashes hold (the launch export, step 17).

# Text files: stored and checked out with LF. Git detects binary files itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats, stated explicitly so they're never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Exported evidence and transcripts: stored exactly as exported, never converted, so their hashes hold.
sessions/** -text
rounds/*/evidence/** -text
